  data: {
    LLM: "1. Drawing and discarding proceed counter-clockwise.\n2. In K'ap Tái Shap, any player can shout 'K'ap!' to take a discard out of turn IF it completes their winning hand (similar to Mahjong).",
    Player: "Welcome to K'ap Tái Shap, the big version for many players! With multiple domino sets in play, finding your 'eye' is easier—but completing four scoring pairs is the real challenge. Watch for discards you need and call 'K'ap!' to grab them out of turn!",
    objective: "Complete a winning hand of five pairs (one identical 'Eye' and four 10/20-sum pairs).",
    gameplay: "1. Drawing and discarding proceed counter-clockwise.\n2. In K'ap Tái Shap, any player can shout 'K'ap!' to take a discard out of turn IF it completes their winning hand (similar to Mahjong).",
    keyRules: [
      'A winning hand requires exactly one identical pair (ngán/eye) from either Civil or Military series',
      'Four additional pairs must each total exactly 10 or 20 pips',
      'The 4-2 tile counts as 3 pips (not 6) when calculating pair totals',
      "Players may call 'K'ap!' to claim a discard out of turn if it completes their hand",
      'First player starts with 10 tiles; others start with 9 tiles',
      'Discards are placed face-up and available for any player to claim',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Typically 6 to 15 players.',
      deck: 'Usually one set per every 2-3 players. For 10 players, 4 sets (128 tiles) is standard.',
      equipment: 'Multiple sets of Chinese dominoes, flat playing surface, chips or counters for stakes',
      dealing: "Standard 10/9 tile split. Tiles are shuffled face-down and built into a long wall (the 'Dragon').",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. Drawing and discarding proceed counter-clockwise.\n2. In K'ap Tái Shap, any player can shout 'K'ap!' to take a discard out of turn IF it completes their winning hand (similar to Mahjong).",
